{"hw":"ἱκετεία","html":"<div class=\"lex-entry\"><h4 class=\"lex-hw gk\">ἱκετεία</h4><span class=\"lex-orth gk\">ἱκετ-εία</span> [<span class=\"gk\">ι], <span class=\"lex-gram\">ἡ</span> </span>, more <span class=\"lex-gram\"> <span class=\"lex-gram\">Att.</span> </span> form of <span class=\"gk\">ἱκεσία</span> (q.v.), <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"1\"><span class=\"lex-n\">A</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">supplication</b>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Th.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1.24</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">ἱκετείαν ποιεῖσθαί τινος</span> to supplicate him, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Id.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">3.67</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">ἱκετεῖαι θεῶν</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">addressed to</b> them, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Lys.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">2.39</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">ἐφ' ἱκετείαν τραπόμενος</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Pl.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Ap.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">39a</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">μετὰ δεήσεως καὶ ἱ</span>. <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">PPetr.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">2p.60</span> </span> <span class=\"lex-cite-date\">(iii B.C.)</span>, cf. <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">SIG</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1181.12</span> </span> (Jewish): pl., <span class=\"gk\">-είας ποιεῖσθαι</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Pl.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Smp.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">183a</span> </span>, etc.</div></div>"}